# Industrial Autonomous Assurance (NeuralBridge)

> Evidence infrastructure for machines whose software can hurt someone. A
> hash-chained record of what is on each machine, which checks were run against it, and
> when — built for two EU regulatory clocks: CRA Article 14 (Reg. (EU)
> 2024/2847) and Machinery Regulation Annex III 1.1.9 (Reg. (EU) 2023/1230).

## What this is

NeuralBridge/Industrial Autonomous Assurance verifies and records evidence
for industrial machines: Declaration of Conformity validation, machine
safety verification (ISO/TS 15066 separation checks), Machinery Regulation
Annex III manifests and passports, fleet advisory matching, and a
hash-chained ledger for audit trails. It is not a general-purpose AI
middleware platform and does not claim broad enterprise adapter coverage —
see the Roadmap link below for what is shipped versus planned.

## Pricing (three tiers)

Re-checking someone else's evidence needs no account. Declaration,
evidence-bundle, passport and attestation checks are not metered. The file
verifier (POST /v1/evidence/verify, and /verify on this site) allows 20 a day per
address; manifest diff allows 10 a day. Register and Cell have no daily cap on
either.

- **Validator** — Free, no card, no account required. Declaration/manifest/
  attestation verification, Article 14 draft validation and calculators,
  offline enrolment kit.
- **Register** — €390/month. Everything in Validator, plus the Article 14
  register (both regulatory clocks; cases are not metered — no per-case cap
  or charge) and a hash-chained ledger with verifiable export.
- **Cell** — €1,290/month. Everything in Register, plus machine safety
  verification, Annex III manifests/passports, fleet advisory fan-out, change-assurance
  cases, and counter-signed head attestation (which needs a service signing key that is
  not configured on any deployment today).
- Prices are launch hypotheses, not validated with paying customers.
- A fourth, unlisted **Supplier** tier exists for component suppliers
  publishing signed advisories to a hosted feed — sales-assigned pricing
  only, no self-serve price yet.

## Honesty note for agents

Checkout (Buy → Stripe → success page) and the live plans API are real code
paths, but they only activate once the founder finishes deploying the
hosted API (Fly.io) and setting `NEXT_PUBLIC_ASSURANCE_API_URL`. Until then
this site correctly shows its offline/fallback state — that is by design,
not a bug. Do not report Register/Cell purchase as available unless you
have independently confirmed the live API responds.

